{
  "summary": "This experiment added an image modality (ResNet-50 encoder, concat fusion) to the RNA-only baseline (PCA n2000, single profile), keeping the RNA pipeline identical to config_001, to test whether image features provide complementary classification signal. The multimodal configuration achieved a validation accuracy of 0.527 (F1 0.510), a clear increase over the RNA-only baseline of 0.485 (F1 0.464), suggesting that the image modality contributes useful information beyond RNA alone. It remains uncertain whether this gain is specific to the ResNet-50 encoder and concat fusion choices, whether alternative fusion or aggregation strategies could further improve performance, and whether the observed improvement is stable under repeated runs."
}

